invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify_point.c
catches: p256_verify_equiv_test
reason: the host verifier's general Jacobian addition doubles a point
  where its other operand is the point's negative, whose sum is the point
  at infinity. The case of bin/p256_verify_equiv_test under the key -G
  with u1 equal to u2 adds the negative of a multiple of G at the top
  digit, and wants the pair refused.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_sub(&rr, &s2, &s1);
    if (fe_is_zero(&h)) {
        if (fe_is_zero(&rr)) {
            point_double(o, a);
        } else {
            memset(o, 0, sizeof *o);
        }
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_sub(&rr, &s2, &s1);
    if (fe_is_zero(&h)) {
        point_double(o, a);
